Question: The annual fee (applicable 2nd year onwards) would be waived off if you spend Rs. 3.5 lakh with the Card within a year. Mean ?
This means that while the credit card may have an annual fee from the second year onwards, you can avoid paying it if you spend ₹3.5 lakh or more in a year using that card.
Example:
1st Year: No annual fee (introductory offer).
2nd Year Onwards:
If you spend ₹3.5 lakh or more in a year → Annual fee is waived (you don't pay anything).
If you spend less than ₹3.5 lakh → Annual fee is charged (as per the bank's terms).
